// @METADATA:name        = variant_distinction_3
// @METADATA:description = True nids vs ni distinction. A nonterminating
//                         loop contains an observe. Under nids (obsntd),
//                         the loop while predicate is an obsntd source
//                         (nonterminating loop node) so it generates
//                         obsntd edges to downstream nodes.
//                         Under ni (obsd), nonterminating loop nodes
//                         are NOT obsd sources — only observe nodes are.
//                         So ni slices the loop but nids keeps it.
// @METADATA:reference   = Constructed to distinguish nids vs ni
// @METADATA:criterion   = x
// @METADATA:expected    = nids: loop kept (while predicate is obsntd
//                         source, generates edges to x and return);
//                         ni: loop may be sliced (while predicate is
//                         NOT obsd source)
// @METADATA:tags        = loop, nontermination, observe, nids-vs-ni,
//                         key-example

coin :~ bernoulli(0.5);
x    :~ bernoulli(0.5);
// Nonterminating loop — coin may always be 1
// while predicate is obsntd source (nids) but NOT obsd source (ni)
while coin = 1 do
    coin :~ bernoulli(0.5);
    x    :~ bernoulli(0.5);
end
// x is set after the loop
observe(x = 1);
z := 99;
return x;